# Repository profile

AQTUATOR — an open-hardware machine repository following [doqs](https://github.com/refaqt/doqs),
included as a submodule at `doqs/`. Read `AGENTS.md` first.

- **Layout is specified, not improvised.** Read `doqs/docs/architecture.md` before adding folders.
  If `doqs/` is empty, run `git submodule update --init --recursive`.
- **Mixed stack:** Python (host software, `software/*`), Arduino/C++ (RP2040 firmware,
  `firmware/*`), Octave (`simulation/cases/*`), FreeCAD (`cad/`).
- Run commands from the repository root. `software/*` are installable packages
  (`pip install -e software/identification`); import them rather than manipulating `sys.path`.
- **Never commit measurement data.** It lives on Google Drive and is indexed by
  `measurement/data-index.csv`. Git LFS here is scoped to CAD binaries only.
- Windows / PowerShell: no `&&`, no bash heredocs, no `cd /d`. See `docs/mistakes/`.
